# docs-coverage.map — Faultline Pro docs coverage manifest (read by docs-drift-check.sh).
#
# FORMAT (one mapping per line):
#   <code-glob> => <doc1.md>[,<doc2.md>,...]
#
#   - <code-glob> : shell glob matched against each git-changed path in the diff
#                   range (case-style glob; ** matches across directories).
#   - =>          : the required mapping operator.
#   - <docN.md>   : one or more comma-separated doc paths that MUST also change in
#                   the SAME range when any code file matches the glob, else RED.
#   - '#'         : comment (whole-line or trailing). Blank lines ignored.
#
# DOC-CLASS is derived from the doc path (arch/design · consumer · changelog · api-ref).
#
# SCOPE: Faultline is a PRODUCT repo (SemVer applies — the code->docs->SemVer loop
# runs here, unlike ASIF-the-knowledge-repo). Conventional-commit -> CHANGELOG.md
# coupling is enforced by the GATE ITSELF (feat/fix/BREAKING in range must touch
# CHANGELOG.md) — so CHANGELOG is intentionally NOT mapped here; do not duplicate it.
#
# DESIGN — conservative Phase-1 map (Gate-9 dogfood onboarding, 2026-07-14):
#   Map only PUBLIC-SURFACE code->doc pairs where a doc is GENUINELY owed when the
#   surface changes (provider set, HTTP API endpoints, compliance coverage, IaC
#   provider). High-churn INTERNALS (scan pipeline, consensus voting math, lib,
#   analysis, services, stores) are intentionally UNMAPPED — mapping them would
#   RED-flag every ordinary refactor and block Phase-2 pre-commit wiring. Expand
#   deliberately as doc<->surface couplings prove stable; start tight.

# --- Provider surface: the installed/verifiable provider set is documented here ---
packages/cli/providers/**              => docs/PROVIDERS.md
packages/api/src/providers/**          => docs/PROVIDERS.md

# --- HTTP API surface: routes ARE the public endpoint reference ---
packages/api/src/routes/**             => packages/api/README.md

# --- Compliance surface: EU AI Act code owes the coverage evidence doc ---
packages/cli/compliance/**             => docs/eu-ai-act-coverage.md

# --- IaC surface: the Terraform provider owes its own README ---
packages/terraform-provider/**         => packages/terraform-provider/README.md

# --- The manifest documents itself: coverage-map edits owe an ARCHITECTURE note ---
# (keeps the onboarding self-describing; mirrors the ASIF dogfood pattern)
docs-coverage.map                      => docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
